<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46105" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subsulto</span></b> , āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq. n.</i>
			[id.], <i>to spring up</i>, <i>to
			leap</i>, <i>jump</i>, <i>hop</i>
			(rare; not in Cic.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas.
				2, 7, 10</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tu subsultas, ego miser vix asto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Capt. 3, 4, 104</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne sermo subsultet imparibus spatiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compositio multis clausulis concisa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					9, 4, 42</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>